      "description": "Careers | UM System Skip to main content Live now: Board of Curators meeting Header: Utility Menu For Employees Rules & Policies News & Events Search Menu Main navigation About Impact Curators President General Counsel Departments & Staff Careers Breadcrumb Home Departments & Staff Human Resources Recruitment Careers Working in the University of Missouri System (UM System) means joining a community that fosters lifelong learning and innovation. We are called to advance health , cultural and social interests of those around us. To aid with your job search, we have compiled resources to help you join our University community or advance the career you already have, across any of our campuses: University of Missouri-Columbia, University of Missouri Health Care, University of Missouri-Kansas City, Missouri University of Science and Technology, University of Missouri-St. Louis or the system’s central administrative offices. Searches Campus Searches UM System campuses list their job openings on separate websites. Please visit the site corresponding to your campus of interest. Faculty and Staff University of Missouri-Columbia (MU) MU Extension University of Missouri Health Care (MU Health) University of Missouri-Kansas City (UMKC) Missouri University of Science and Technology (Missouri S&T) University of Missouri-St. Louis (UMSL) Students MU MU Health UMKC Missouri S&T UMSL Central Administrative Offices Searches Job listings for central administrative offices are posted within the MU find a job tool, which includes listings for MU, MU Extension and UM System. To review the department to which you’re applying, please check the hiring department on each vacancy notice. Job listings for Current Staff Job listings for Prospective Staff Systemwide Executive Searches The University of Missouri System Executive Recruitment team conducts executive searches for key positions. Visit the Executive Searches webpage for more information about current openings. Section Menu Recruitment Careers Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Executive Searches H-1B Sponsorship Guidelines & Eligibility Standards Systemwide Search Committee Training The Systemwide Search Committee Training in Percipio provides strategic and tactical advice to search committees of academic/faculty, academic administrator or executive searches for recruiting colleagues to the University. The focus is on best and common practices in recruiting broadly, while ensuring compliance with University rules and regulations. If you have a disability defined by the Americans with Disabilities Act, Collected Rules and Regulations Section 600.080: Policy Related to Employees with Disabilities , requiring specific accommodations to complete this training, please contact the HR Service Center at hrservicecenter@umsystem.edu . Contact Us University of Missouri System Contact Information Information For Business Partners Media Current Employees Past Employees Prospective Employees Quick Links Careers & Employment Equal Opportunity Title IX Executive Searches UM Academic Technology File an Open Records Request Footer: Social Media Links Facebook Instagram Linkedin X Youtube University of Missouri System is an equal opportunity employer . Copyright | Accessibility | Careers and Employment | Emergency Notification | Privacy Policy © Copyright 2026 by The Curators of the University of Missouri, a public corporation."
